<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  pnpm demo:offline (OF-BLD-012 §8.1): the JATS the fixture-mode service
  returns for B5 (PMC8471596). THIS IS NOT THE PAPER. It is the structural
  document tests/fixtures/jats/structural.xml — a made-up article SHAPE for
  testing the parser — standing in until the real one is saved here. The
  sandbox this was written in could not reach Europe PMC. To replace it:

    curl -sS -A 'openferment-core/0.1' \
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8471596/fullTextXML \
      > core/tests/fixtures/demo/jats/PMC8471596.xml

  then regenerate extract/B5.json with a key (see README, 'The offline demo').
-->
<!--
  STRUCTURAL FIXTURE. THIS IS NOT A PAPER.

  A minimal JATS document whose only purpose is to pin what `split_jats` does
  with each element the real corpus uses: an abstract, nested sections, a
  table kept as rows, a figure caption, inline sup/sub, a licence, and the
  three back-matter elements that must be dropped. Every sentence is
  placeholder prose about an imaginary organism and an imaginary run; nothing
  here is a measurement of anything, and nothing here may be quoted as one.

  The real fixture is tests/fixtures/jats/PMC8471596.xml (B5, MDPI Life, CC
  BY), checked in once from Europe PMC. test_intake.py tests that file when
  it is present and this one always.
-->
<article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article">
  <front>
    <article-meta>
      <title-group>
        <article-title>A structural fixture for the Intake parser</article-title>
      </title-group>
      <permissions>
        <license license-type="open-access" xlink:href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">
          <license-p>This is an open access article distributed under a placeholder licence.</license-p>
        </license>
      </permissions>
      <abstract abstract-type="graphical">
        <p>A picture of nothing.</p>
      </abstract>
      <abstract>
        <p>The   abstract  comes first,   whatever order the   elements appear in.</p>
      </abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec id="sec1">
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>An imaginary organism was grown in an imaginary vessel.</p>
      <p>Its rate is written per litre, as in mg L<sup>-1</sup>, and its gas as CO<sub>2</sub>.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="sec2">
      <title>Results</title>
      <p>Results have a preamble of their own.</p>
      <sec id="sec2.1">
        <title>Growth</title>
        <p>The nested section flattens with the parent heading in front of it.</p>
        <table-wrap id="tab1">
          <label>Table 1</label>
          <caption><p>Placeholder rows, kept as rows.</p></caption>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Condition</th><th>Value</th><th>Unit</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Placeholder A</td><td>7</td><td>mg L<sup>-1</sup></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Placeholder B</td><td>9</td><td>mg L<sup>-1</sup></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </table-wrap>
        <fig id="fig1">
          <label>Figure 1</label>
          <caption><p>A placeholder figure caption.</p></caption>
          <graphic xlink:href="nothing.png"/>
        </fig>
      </sec>
      <sec id="sec2.2">
        <title>Empty</title>
        <sec id="sec2.2.1">
          <title>Deeper</title>
          <p>Three levels down, still prefixed all the way up.</p>
        </sec>
      </sec>
    </sec>
  </body>
  <back>
    <ack><p>Acknowledgements must not become a section.</p></ack>
    <fn-group><fn><p>A footnote must not become a section.</p></fn></fn-group>
    <ref-list>
      <title>References</title>
      <ref id="r1"><mixed-citation>A reference must not become a section.</mixed-citation></ref>
    </ref-list>
  </back>
</article>
